"gloss":"small"},{"text":"நறு","lemma":"நறு","gloss":"fragrant"}],"gloss":"small and fragrant"},{"surface":"முஞ்ஞை","parts":[{"text":"முஞ்ஞை","lemma":"முஞ்ஞை","gloss":"muññai shrub"}],"gloss":"muññai shrub"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"முயல்வந்து","parts":[{"text":"முயல்","lemma":"முயல்","gloss":"hare"},{"text":"வந்து","lemma":"வா","gloss":"having come"}],"gloss":"hare coming"},{"surface":"கறிக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"கறிக்கும்","lemma":"கறி","gloss":"nibbling"}],"gloss":"nibbling"},{"surface":"முன்றில்","parts":[{"text":"முன்றில்","lemma":"முன்றில்","gloss":"front yard"}],"gloss":"front yard"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சீறூர்","parts":[{"text":"சீறூர்","lemma":"சீறூர்","gloss":"small village"}],"gloss":"small village","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மன்னனைப்","parts":[{"text":"மன்னனைப்","lemma":"மன்னனைப்","gloss":"the chief"}],"gloss":"the chief","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பாடினை","parts":[{"text":"பாடினை","lemma":"பாடு","gloss":"if you sing of"}],"gloss":"if you sing of"},{"surface":"செலினே","parts":[{"text":"செலின்","lemma":"செல்","gloss":"if you go"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"if you go indeed"}]}],"literal":"... near the forest situated / In the small village of dry lands, paddy does not grow indeed. / Millet and foxtail millet, all those that existed, / were exhausted by giving to the begging people. / ... he is content. / Even though he is such, O bard, greatly / in the large bowl, poured milk, inside ... / like the sourness of wild berries, ripe ... / ... dried meat, fatty piece, / with the rice of harvested ears, pouring ghee, having cooked, / thick white rice well-stirred with the ladle, / having eaten and stayed happily, afterwards ... / ... he will give indeed! / Where the small fragrant muññai shrub grows tall at the base of the tāḷi plant, / in the front yard where hares come to nibble, / if you go singing of the chief of this small village.","translation":"In this small dry-land village bordering the forest, paddy does not grow. Even the millet and foxtail millet they had have been completely exhausted, given away to needy suppliants. Yet, O bard, if you go singing of the chief of this small village—whose front yard is visited by hares that come to nibble on the small, fragrant muññai shrubs growing tall beside the tāḷi plants—he will surely welcome you. He will serve you thick, white rice cooked with ghee and harvested grains, stirred well with a ladle, along with rich, fatty pieces of dried meat and sour wild-berry relish mixed with milk in a large bowl. After you eat and rest happily, he will surely give you grand gifts.","modern":"காட்டை ஒட்டியுள்ள புன்புலத்துச் சிறிய ஊரில் நெல் விளையாது. இருந்த வரகும் தினையும் இரவலர்களுக்குக் கொடுத்துத் தீர்ந்துவிட்டன. அவன் வறியவன் ஆயினும், பாணனே! தாளிச் செடியின் அடியில் வளர்ந்த சிறிய நறிய முஞ்ஞை தழைகளை முற்றத்தில் முயல்கள் வந்து மேயும் சிறிய ஊர்த் தலைவனை நீ பாடிச் சென்றால், அவன் உனக்கு நெய் பெய்து சமைத்த வெண்சோற்றையும், கொழுத்த இறைச்சித் துண்டுகளையும், பாலும் புளிப்பும் கலந்த உணவையும் தருவான். உண்டு மகிழ்ந்த பின் உனக்குப் பரிசில்களையும் தருவான்.","explanation":"This poem is addressed to a wandering bard by an observer who praises the boundless generosity of a local chief. The chief lives in a small, impoverished dry-land village where paddy cannot grow, and even his millet reserves have been exhausted by feeding previous visitors. Despite his poverty, he possesses a noble heart and will go to great lengths to feed any new guest with rich, ghee-cooked rice, fatty dried meat, and a sour berry-milk curry. The setting belongs to the vākai tiṇai, specifically the theme of mūtiṉ mullai, which celebrates the traditional hospitality and warrior pride of ancient households. The peaceful image of wild hares entering the front yard to nibble on fragrant muññai shrubs highlights the rustic simplicity of the chief's home, contrasting beautifully with his grand spirit of giving.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.15,0.7],[0.7,1.0],[1.0,